    "field": "Paleoclimatology",
    "problem": "General circulation models have failed to simulate the observed 25-fold increase in dust deposition over Antarctica during glacial periods, a shortcoming attributed to an incomplete understanding of how dust sources and atmospheric transport processes are coupled to climate.",
    "method": "The authors propose that the ~25-fold increase in glacial dust flux is caused by stronger South American dust sources, combined with a longer atmospheric lifetime for dust particles resulting from a reduced hydrological cycle during the ice ages.",
    "task": "The task is to analyze an 800,000-year aeolian dust record from the EPICA Dome C ice core to understand the relationship between atmospheric dust deposition in Antarctica and climate changes over eight glacial-interglacial cycles.",
